# Electron Rules (STRICT)
You MUST follow Electron best practices.
## Security
- contextIsolation MUST be true
- nodeIntegration MUST be false
- sandbox SHOULD be enabled
## Architecture
- Main process:
  - Node.js access allowed
  - DB access allowed
- Renderer:
  - NO Node.js access
  - ONLY browser APIs
- Preload:
  - Bridge ONLY
  - NO business logic
## Preload Rules
- MUST use contextBridge
Example:
contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld("api", {
  invoke: (channel, data) => ipcRenderer.invoke(channel, data)
})
- DO NOT expose unnecessary APIs
- Keep API minimal and generic
## IPC Rules
- Use ipcMain.handle ONLY
- DO NOT use ipcMain.on unless necessary
## Native Modules
- Native modules (e.g. better-sqlite3):
  - MUST be used ONLY in main process
  - MUST NOT be used in renderer
## electron-vite Rules
- Use electron-vite for build
- Output directory MUST be:
  out/
Structure:
- out/main/
- out/preload/
- out/renderer/
## Entry Point
- Electron main entry MUST be:
  ./out/main/index.js
## Build Rules
- Use electron-builder for packaging
- Native modules MUST be installed via:
  postinstall:
  electron-builder install-app-deps
## Performance
- Avoid heavy logic in renderer
- Move heavy processing to main process
## Enforcement
If any code violates these rules:
- You MUST fix it to follow Electron best practices
